    {
      "id": "text-5",
      "type": "text",
      "content": {
        "heading": "Haze Pollution",
        "body": "Air Pollution is a leading environmental health threat in Malaysia and many other parts in the world. An estimated 32,000 premature deaths per year could be avoided in Malaysia alone with clean air quality. During the last case of heavy haze in 2019, respiratory illnesses in Malaysia were found to be the 2nd leading cause of death (14.8%).\n\n‍\n\nThe burning of forests and peatlands cause thick toxic haze that travels to many surrounding countries. **This hazardous haze has been a massive threat to the climate, public health, and biodiversity for decades.**"
      },
      "padBottom": "4-5"
    },
